 The preferred CryptPad bundle includes web-apps, onlyoffice-editor, its separate RequireJS vendor input, licenses and build recipes at one exact commit. Upstream fonts are excluded. Reviewed fonts are supplied through the separate license manifest. Runtime compression is regenerated and verified after all final UI and font modifications. SDK, deployed UI assets and compression checks do not certify auxiliary WASM, x2t reproduction, the complete editor or a proprietary hosted service's legal boundary.
 
 Generated deployable assets missing from the imported static bundle are materialized from the preferred UI build through the shared runtime selector. Debug source maps are excluded. The final compact manifest is refreshed before distribution and split-pack identity is recorded.
+
+The compact dictionary profile is defined once by the runtime asset selector.
+The preferred UI build derives spell/hyphen capabilities from those selected
+real dictionary files, materializes the native `hyph_<locale>.dic` path from
+the original dictionary bytes, and configures the native language provider
+before each main editor API is constructed. Unsupported document languages are
+not relabeled. UI output is materialized from preferred-source compilation,
+including regenerated compression, rather than retaining copied generated UI.
